    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1023">

                <pb facs="0888" n="876" xml:id="pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51/882: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-06T17:00:00-05:00">June 6, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. The Provisional President last night expressed appreciation of our
                    Government’s confidence in his administration as evidenced by export-import
                    credit.</p>
                <p>Dr. Cordova and the Minister for Defense<anchor n="62" xml:id="d1023-f1"/>
                    believe that the highway construction work ought to be done by a responsible
                    foreign preferably American company with most positions given to Ecuadorans and
                    Ecuadoran engineers cooperating.</p>
                <p>Despatch by air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1023-f1" n="62" xml:id="d1023-f1-content">
